# close_rules.tsv — which close checks a rotation's changes call for (read by .claude/rotation/close_plan.sh)
#
# one check per line, tab-separated; `-` = none. columns:
#   name        the check (also the key in the verdict)
#   paths       trigger globs, `;`-separated; `!glob` excludes; `**` crosses `/`, `*` does not; `-` = no own trigger
#   artifact    what it reads (a label the project chooses, e.g. release-build / dev-build / -); every running check
#               pulls in its `needs`
#   stamp       <x>[:<tool>] — <ROTATION_STAMP_DIR>/<x>-latest.json and the `tool` name in stamps.jsonl (tool defaults to x);
#               `-` = no stamp (a prerequisite row)
#   minutes     typical duration
#   mode        sync (the next rotation waits for it) / async (runs beside the next rotation) / - (prerequisite: takes its dependants' mode)
#   sync_paths  globs whose hit turns an async check sync for this close
#   needs       a prerequisite check (a row with stamp `-`)
#   show        stamp keys the verdict's result section lists, `,`-separated (dotted = nested)
#   regress     <key>:down|up|nonzero — red when the reading moved that way against the previous stamp; `~` prefix = amber;
#               <key>:each-up:<rel>[:<k>[:<ceiling>]] — per entry of a map of repeated readings (docs/data.md)
#
# decision per check: diff(<its stamp's headSha>..HEAD) hits `paths` → run; else carried from that sha.
# a missing stamp, a -dirty sha, a sha not in the repo, or a red verdict → run. no thresholds: the table is the rule.
# a row named in rotation.conf ROTATION_CLOSE_CHECKS_OFF is dropped before planning: no verdict row, no judgement.
# start wide (the whole source tree triggers the sweep); narrow it from stamp history.
#
#name	paths	artifact	stamp	minutes	mode	sync_paths	needs	show	regress
build	-	-	-	2	-	-	-	-	-
sweep	src/**;tests/**	release-build	sweep	9	async	-	build	pass,passTotal,harnessError	pass:down;passTotal:down;harnessError:nonzero
bench	src/**;bench/**	release-build	bench	18	async	bench/**	build	median	-
